= 1 The archipelago

The Kestrel Islands are an archipelago of five inhabited islands in the Ashwind
Sea, roughly 400 km from the nearest mainland harbour. They are the rim of a
drowned volcanic crater; the crater floor between them, the Kestrel Deep,
reaches 890 m at its deepest sounding.

